{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nI am writing from Cologne, tired but content. The journey has been a mix of rain and reflection. In Koblenz, I waited out the absence of Councillor Lange, which gave me time to sit with my thoughts. Yesterday, I took the boat to Neuwied to visit the Moravian Sisters. Their quiet devotion is striking; one sees the ethical life in its simplest, most earnest form.\n\nThis morning, the rain was heavy as I boarded the Rhine steamer. I stopped at Linz to view a painting in a hilltop church, as Schulze advised. It was worth the climb. In Bonn, I called on Windischmann and his son-in-law Walther. We spoke, and the wine was good.\n\nI think of you and the boys here in Berlin. The river moves on, and so do I, but my heart remains with you. Do not worry about my health; the change of air is doing me good. I shall write again soon.\n\nYour loving,\nG. W. F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795080192,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":223,"prompt_tokens":952,"total_tokens":1175,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-vmxmp5RsBiMADzJ8PNeFCUlsd7szYcD0","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":952,"prompt_ms":893.468,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.938516806722689,"prompt_per_second":1065.5110199805702,"predicted_n":223,"predicted_ms":5254.722,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.669918918918917,"predicted_per_second":42.24771548333099}}